  84 \\times 12 = (80 + 4)(10 + 2) = 80 \\times 10 + 80 \\times 2 + 4 \\times 10 + 4 \\times 2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 800 + 160 + 40 + 8 = 1008\n   \\]\n\n2. **Standard multiplication**:\n   \\[\n   84 \\times 12 = 8 \\text{ hundreds, } 4 \\text{ tens} \\times 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 960 + 48 = 1008\n   \\]\n\n3. **Alternative approach**:\n   \\[\n   84 \\times 10 = 840 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 84 \\times 2 = 168\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   840 + 168 = 1008\n   \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{1008}\\).",
