m that the product is 4095. I think that's solid. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 45 and 91 is \\boxed{4095}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 45 and 91, we can break down the multiplication into simpler steps:\n\n1. Recognize that 91 can be expressed as 90 + 1.\n2. Use the distributive property: \\(45 \\times 91 = 45 \\times (90 + 1)\\).\n3. Calculate each part separately:\n   - \\(45 \\times 90 = 4050\\)\n   - \\(45 \\times 1 = 45\\)\n4. Add the results together: \\(4050 + 45 = 4095\\).\n\nAnother method involves breaking down the multiplication using the standard algorithm:\n1. Multiply 45 by the units digit (1) of 91: \\(45 \\times 1 = 45\\).\n2. Multiply 45 by the tens digit (9), shifting the result one position to the left: \\(45 \\times 9 = 405\\), then add a zero: \\(4050\\).\n3. Add the two results: \\(45 + 4050 = 4095\\).\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 45 and 91 is \\(\\boxed{4095}\\).",
