-\n 91  (91 x 1)\n 364 (91 x 4, shifted one position to the left)\n----\n3731\n\nBut when I add 91 and 3640, I get 4551. That's not matching. So where did I go wrong?\n\nAh! Wait, no. Because when you multiply 91 by 41, the second step is 91 x 4 = 364, but since it's the tens place, you have to add a zero. So 364 becomes 3640. Then adding 91 + 3640. But 91 + 3640 is 3731. Wait, but 91 + 3640 is 3731? Let me check:\n\n3640 + 91. 3640 + 90 is 3730, then +1 is 3731. Yes. But when I did the distributive property earlier, I got 3731. So that's correct. But when I thought of adding 91 and 3640, I thought 91 + 3640 is 4551, which is wrong. So that was my mistake. So actually, both methods give 3731. So that's the correct answer.\n\nWait, but let me verify with another method. Let's do 91 x 41. Maybe breaking down 41 into 40 +1, so 91*(40 +1) = 91*40 + 91*1. 91*40 is 3640, and 91*1 is 91. Then 3640 +91 is 3731. Yes, that's the same as before. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another multiplication technique. Let's try multiplying 91 by 41 using the standard algorithm:\n\n      91\n   x 41\n   ----\n      91  (91 x 1)\n     364   (91 x 4, shifted left by one)\n   ----\n    3731\n\nYes, that's correct. So the product is 3731.\n\nWait, but just to make sure, maybe do the multiplication the long way:\n\n91\nx41\n----\n91\n364\n----\n3731\n\nYes, adding 91 and 3640 gives 3731. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator to check. But since I don't have a calculator, let me verify with another method. Let's compute 91 x 41:\n\n91 x 40 is 3640, and 91 x1 is 91. So 3640 +91 = 3731. Yep, that's the same.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 91 is 14*6.5 and 41 is 41, but that seems more complicated. Probably not helpful.\n\nAlternatively, use the difference of squares formula? Hmm, 91 and 41. Wait, 91 is 40 + 51, and 41 is 40 - 9. Not sure if that helps.\n\nAlternatively, 91 x41 = (90 +1)(40 +1) = 90*40 +90*1 +1*40 +1*1 = 3600 +90 +40 +1 = 3600 +131 = 3731. Yep, same result.\n\nSo all methods lead to 3731. Therefore, the product of 91 and 41 is 3731.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 91 and 41 is \\boxed{3731}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 91 and 41, we can use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n91 \\times 41 = (90 + 1)(40 + 1)\n\\]\n\nExpanding this using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n(90 + 1)(40 + 1) = 90 \\times 40 + 90 \\times 1 + 1 \\times 40 + 1 \\times 1\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n\\[\n90 \\times 40 = 3600\n\\]\n\\[\n90 \\times 1 = 90\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\times 40 = 40\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\times 1 = 1\n\\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\n\\[\n3600 + 90 + 40 + 1 = 3600 + 131 = 3731\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify this by standard multiplication:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n 91 \\\\\n\\times 41 \\\\\n\\hline\n 91 \\quad \\text{(91 multiplied by 1)} \\\\\n3640 \\quad \\text{(91 multiplied by 4, shifted one position to the left)} \\\\\n\\hline\n3731 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAdding the partial products:\n\n\\[\n91 + 3640 = 3731\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 91 and 41 is \\(\\boxed{3731}\\).",
