et's do it the standard way:\n\n     84\n   x 33\n   ----\n     252  (84 x 3)\n   2400   (84 x 30, shifted one position to the left)\n   ----\n   2772\n\nWait, let me write it out step by step. Multiplying 84 by 33:\n\nFirst, multiply 84 by 3 (the units digit of 33). 84 x 3 = 252. Then, multiply 84 by 30 (the tens digit, which is 30, so we write it down as 30 and add a zero). So, 84 x 30 = 2520. Then, add 252 and 2520. 252 + 2520 = 2772. Yep, that's the same as before. \n\nAlternatively, if I do it as (80 + 4)(30 + 3) = 80*30 + 80*3 + 4*30 + 4*3 = 2400 + 240 + 120 + 12 = 2400 + 240 is 2640, plus 120 is 2760, plus 12 is 2772. All right, so every method I try gives me 2772. \n\nI think that's solid. Let me just check with a calculator to be 100% sure. But since I don't have a calculator here, maybe approximate. If 80*30=2400, and 80*3=240, 4*30=120, 4*3=12. Adding all together: 2400+240=2640, 2640+120=2760, 2760+12=2772. Yep, same answer. So, I think that's correct. \n\nTherefore, the product of 84 and 33 is 2772.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 84 and 33 can be calculated using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n84 \\times 33 = (80 + 4) \\times (30 + 3) = 80 \\times 30 + 80 \\times 3 + 4 \\times 30 + 4 \\times 3\n\\]\n\nBreaking down each term:\n- \\(80 \\times 30 = 2400\\)\n- \\(80 \\times 3 = 240\\)\n- \\(4 \\times 30 = 120\\)\n- \\(4 \\times 3 = 12\\)\n\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n2400 + 240 + 120 + 12 = 2772\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 84 and 33 is \\(\\boxed{2772}\\).",
