I don't see any mistakes in my reasoning here. Each step checks out. So I'm confident that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 30 and 98 is \\boxed{2940}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 30 and 98, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Breaking down 98**:\n   - \\( 98 = 100 - 2 \\)\n   - \\( 30 \\times 98 = 30 \\times (100 - 2) = 30 \\times 100 - 30 \\times 2 = 3000 - 60 = 2940 \\)\n\n2. **Standard multiplication algorithm**:\n   - Multiply 30 by 8: \\( 30 \\times 8 = 240 \\)\n   - Multiply 30 by 90: \\( 30 \\times 90 = 2700 \\)\n   - Add the results: \\( 240 + 2700 = 2940 \\)\n\n3. **Using distributive property**:\n   - \\( 30 \\times 98 = (3 \\times 10) \\times 98 = 3 \\times (10 \\times 98) = 3 \\times 980 = 2940 \\)\n\n4. **Alternative method**:\n   - \\( 30 \\times 98 = 3 \\times 10 \\times 98 = 3 \\times 98 = 294 \\)\n   - Multiply by 10: \\( 294 \\times 10 = 2940 \\)\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 30 and 98 is \\(\\boxed{2940}\\).",
