ess than the estimates, the actual product should be a bit less than 4500. 4089 is indeed less, so that makes sense. If I had done 90 times 50, which is 4500, and subtracted the difference: 90 is 3 less than 90, and 50 is 3 more than 47. Wait, maybe that's complicating. Alternatively, the difference between 90 and 87 is 3, and between 50 and 47 is 3. So maybe using the formula (a - b)(c + d) or something else. But since all my manual calculations give me 4089, and the estimation is reasonable, I think that's the right answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking down 47 into 40 + 7 again. 87 times 40 is 3480, and 87 times 7 is 609. Then, adding 3480 + 609. Let's see, 3480 + 600 is 4080, plus 9 is 4089. Yep, same result. So all methods converge to 4089. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 87 and 47 is 4089.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 87 and 47 is \\boxed{4089}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 87 and 47, we can use the distributive property:\n\n1. Break down 87 into \\(80 + 7\\) and 47 into \\(40 + 7\\).\n2. Multiply each part:\n   - \\(80 \\times 40 = 3200\\)\n   - \\(80 \\times 7 = 560\\)\n   - \\(7 \\times 40 = 280\\)\n   - \\(7 \\times 7 = 49\\)\n3. Add all the results together:\n   - \\(3200 + 560 + 280 + 49 = 3200 + 560 = 3760\\)\n   - \\(3760 + 280 = 4040\\)\n   - \\(4040 + 49 = 4089\\)\n\nWe can also verify this using the standard multiplication method:\n1. Multiply 7 by 7: \\(7 \\times 7 = 49\\) (write down 9, carry over 4)\n2. Multiply 7 by 4: \\(7 \\times 4 = 28\\) plus the carried over 4 gives 32 (write down 32)\n3. Multiply 8 by 7: \\(8 \\times 7 = 56\\) (write down 56, carry over 0)\n4. Multiply 8 by 4: \\(8 \\times 4 = 32\\) (write down 32, carry over 0)\n5. Combine the results: 329, 560, and 3200, then add them up:\n   - \\(3200 + 329 = 3529\\)\n   - \\(3529 + 560 = 4089\\)\n\nAnother verification using the difference of squares approach:\n1. Break down 87 into \\(90 - 3\\) and 47 into \\(50 - 3\\).\n2. Expand \\((90 - 3)(50 - 3)\\):\n   - \\(90 \\times 50 = 4500\\)\n   - \\(90 \\times (-3) = -270\\)\n   - \\((-3) \\times 50 = -150\\)\n   - \\((-3) \\times (-3) = 9\\)\n3. Combine the results:\n   - \\(4500 - 270 - 150 + 9 = 4500 - 420 + 9 = 4089\\)\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 87 and 47 is \\(\\boxed{4089}\\).",
