\(16 \\times (70 + 3)\\):\n     \\[\n     16 \\times 70 + 16 \\times 3 = 1120 + 48 = 1168\n     \\]\n\n3. **Verifying with vertical multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     73 \\\\\n   \\times 16 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     438 \\quad (\\text{73} \\times 6) \\\\\n   1120 \\quad (\\text{73} \\times 10) \\\\\n   \\hline\n     1168 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Alternative method using addition:**\n   - Break down 73 into 70 and 3, then multiply each by 16 and add:\n     \\[\n     16 \\times 70 + 16 \\times 3 = 1120 + 48 = 1168\n     \\]\n\nAll methods consistently result in the product of 16 and 73 being \\(\\boxed{1168}\\).",
