4500 - 270 is 4230, plus 100 is 4330, minus 6 is 4324. Again, same answer. So that's three different methods giving me 4324. Seems like that's the right answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator to check. But since I don't have a calculator here, I can do a quick check. Let's see, 92 times 47. Let's break it down again. 92*40 is 3680, and 92*7 is 644. 3680 + 644. 3680 + 600 is 4280, plus 44 is 4324. Yep, same result. So I think that's correct. So the product of 92 and 47 is 4324. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I think that's the answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 92 and 47 is \\boxed{4324}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 92 and 47, we can use the distributive property:\n\nFirst, break down the numbers:\n- \\(92 = 90 + 2\\)\n- \\(47 = 40 + 7\\)\n\nMultiply each part separately:\n1. \\(90 \\times 40 = 3600\\)\n2. \\(90 \\times 7 = 630\\)\n3. \\(2 \\times 40 = 80\\)\n4. \\(2 \\times 7 = 14\\)\n\nAdd all the results together:\n\\[\n3600 + 630 + 80 + 14 = 4324\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method:\n1. Multiply 92 by 47 using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n   - \\(7 \\times 92 = 644\\)\n   - \\(40 \\times 92 = 3680\\)\n   - Add the results: \\(644 + 3680 = 4324\\)\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 92 and 47 is \\(\\boxed{4324}\\).",
