oduct of 44 and 32 is \\boxed{1408}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 44 and 32, we can use the distributive property. \n\nFirst, break down the numbers into their tens and ones places:\n- 44 can be split into 40 and 4.\n- 32 can be split into 30 and 2.\n\nUsing the distributive property:\n\\[\n(40 + 4) \\times (30 + 2) = 40 \\times 30 + 40 \\times 2 + 4 \\times 30 + 4 \\times 2\n\\]\n\nCalculate each part step by step:\n- \\(40 \\times 30 = 1200\\)\n- \\(40 \\times 2 = 80\\)\n- \\(4 \\times 30 = 120\\)\n- \\(4 \\times 2 = 8\\)\n\nAdd all the results together:\n\\[\n1200 + 80 + 120 + 8 = 1280 + 120 + 8 = 1400 + 8 = 1408\n\\]\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication method:\n\\[\n44 \\times 32 = (44 \\times 2) + (44 \\times 30) = 88 + 1320 = 1408\n\\]\n\nAnother verification using the difference of squares formula:\n- Recognize that \\(44 = 4 \\times 11\\) and \\(32 = 8 \\times 4\\)\n- Then, \\(44 \\times 32 = 4 \\times 8 \\times 11 = 32 \\times 11 = 320 + 32 = 352\\). Wait, this seems incorrect. Let me check again.\n\nWait, actually, \\(44 \\times 32\\) can be calculated as:\n- \\(44 \\times 32 = (40 + 4) \\times 32 = 40 \\times 32 + 4 \\times 32\\)\n- \\(40 \\times 32 = 1280\\)\n- \\(4 \\times 32 = 128\\)\n- Adding these results: \\(1280 + 128 = 1408\\)\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 44 and 32 is \\(\\boxed{1408}\\).",
