y, maybe use a calculator to verify. But since I don't have a calculator here, I need to rely on my mental math. Let me try another way. 13 is 10 + 3, so 94*13 = 94*10 + 94*3. Which is 940 + 282. 940 + 200 is 1140, plus 82 is 1222. Yep, same answer. So I think that's correct.\n\nWait, just to check, maybe I can reverse the numbers. 13*94. Let's see, 13*90=1170, 13*4=52, so 1170+52=1222. Same result. Okay, so all methods point to 1222. I think that's the right answer. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. So the product of 94 and 13 is 1222.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 94 and 13 is \\boxed{1222}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 94 and 13, we can use the distributive property. \n\nFirst, break down 94 into 90 and 4:\n- Calculate \\( 90 \\times 13 \\):\n  - \\( 90 \\times 10 = 900 \\)\n  - \\( 90 \\times 3 = 270 \\)\n  - Adding these results: \\( 900 + 270 = 1170 \\)\n\n- Calculate \\( 4 \\times 13 \\):\n  - \\( 4 \\times 10 = 40 \\)\n  - \\( 4 \\times 3 = 12 \\)\n  - Adding these results: \\( 40 + 12 = 52 \\)\n\n- Add the two results together: \\( 1170 + 52 = 1222 \\)\n\nTo verify, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n- Multiply 94 by 3: \\( 94 \\times 3 = 282 \\)\n- Multiply 94 by 10: \\( 94 \\times 10 = 940 \\)\n- Add the results: \\( 940 + 282 = 1222 \\)\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 94 and 13 is \\(\\boxed{1222}\\).",
