ubtract 80 once (since 69 is 70 -1) to get 5600 -80 = 5520. Same answer.\n\nSo, all methods lead to 5520. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 69 and 80 is 5520.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 69 and 80 is \\boxed{5520}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 69 and 80, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Breaking down the numbers**:\n   - Recognize that 69 is 70 - 1.\n   - Calculate \\(70 \\times 80 = 5600\\).\n   - Subtract 1 times 80 from this result: \\(5600 - 80 = 5520\\).\n\n2. **Standard multiplication**:\n   - Multiply 69 by 80 by breaking it into \\(69 \\times 8 \\times 10\\).\n   - First, calculate \\(69 \\times 8\\):\n     - \\(60 \\times 8 = 480\\)\n     - \\(9 \\times 8 = 72\\)\n     - Add the results: \\(480 + 72 = 552\\).\n   - Then multiply by 10: \\(552 \\times 10 = 5520\\).\n\n3. **Distributive property**:\n   - Use the distributive property: \\(69 \\times 80 = (70 - 1) \\times 80\\).\n   - Calculate \\(70 \\times 80 = 5600\\) and subtract \\(1 \\times 80 = 80\\): \\(5600 - 80 = 5520\\).\n\n4. **Verification**:\n   - Confirm using different methods (vertical multiplication, repeated addition) to ensure consistency.\n\nAll methods consistently lead to the same result. Therefore, the product of 69 and 80 is \\(\\boxed{5520}\\).",
