      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 91 and 76. Hmm, let's see. I remember that multiplying two-digit numbers can sometimes be done by breaking them down into smaller parts. Maybe I can use the method where you split the numbers into tens and ones. Let me try that.\n\nFirst, let's take 91. If I split that into tens and ones, it's 90 + 1. Similarly, 76 can be split into 70 + 6. So, the problem becomes multiplying (90 + 1) by (70 + 6). I think this is called the distributive property, right? So, I can expand this using the distributive property, which is a(b + c) = ab + ac.\n\nLet me write that out step by step. \n\nFirst, multiply 90 by 70. That should be straightforward. 90 times 70. Hmm, 9 times 7 is 63, and then we have two zeros from the tens and hundreds place, so 6300. Okay, that's 6300.\n\nNext, multiply 90 by 6. That's 90 times 6. 9 times 6 is 54, and again with the two zeros, so 5400. Wait, no, hold on. Wait, 90 times 6 is 540, right? Because 90 is 9 tens, so 9 tens times 6 is 54 tens, which is 540. Then add the two parts together: 6300 + 5400. Let me check that. 6300 + 5400. 6000 + 5000 is 11,000, and 300 + 400 is 700, so total is 11,700. Okay, that's the first part.\n\nNow, the second part of the multiplication is 1 times 70 and 1 times 6. So, 1 times 70 is 70, and 1 times 6 is 6. Adding those together gives 70 + 6 = 76.\n\nNow, add all the parts together: 6300 + 5400 + 76. Wait, no, hold on. Wait, actually, when you use the distributive property, you have (90 + 1)(70 + 6) = 90*70 + 90*6 + 1*70 + 1*6. So, that's 6300 + 5400 + 70 + 6. So, adding those up: 6300 + 5400 is 11,700, then 70 + 6 is 76. So, 11,700 + 76 = 11,776. So, the total product is 11,776. Let me verify that with another method to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do the standard multiplication method. Let's try that. Multiply 91 by 76. \n\nStarting with the ones digit of 76, which is 6. Multiply 91 by 6. 90*6=540, and 1*6=6, so 540 + 6 = 546. So, that's the ones place. Then, multiply 91 by the tens digit, which is 7, but since it's in the tens place, it's actually 70. So, 91*70. 90*70=6300, and 1*70=70. So, 6300 + 70 = 6370. Now, add that to the previous result: 546 + 6370. Let's do that. 546 + 6370. 500 + 6300 = 6800, 46 + 70 = 116. So, 6800 + 116 = 6916. Wait, that's different from the previous answer. Hmm, so now I have two different results. That means I must have made a mistake somewhere.\n\nWait, let me check again. First method: (90 + 1)(70 + 6) = 90*70 + 90*6 + 1*70 + 1*6. 90*70 is 6300, 90*6 is 540, 1*70 is 70, 1*6 is 6. Adding those: 6300 + 540 = 6840, then 6840 + 70 = 6910, then 6910 + 6 = 6916. Wait, so in my first calculation, I added 6300 + 5400 first, which was 11,700, then added 76 to get 11,776. But that was wrong. Wait, why did I do that? Because I thought the first part was 6300 + 5400, but actually, the first part is 90*70 + 90*6, which is 6300 + 540 = 6840. Then adding 1*70 + 1*6 = 76. So, 6840 + 76 = 6916. So, my first calculation was wrong because I added 6300 + 5400 instead of adding 6300 + 540. So, that was a mistake. So, the correct total is 6916. \n\nBut then, when I did the standard multiplication, I got 6916 as well. So, that's consistent. So, the correct answer is 6916. So, where did I go wrong in my first calculation? Let me see. Initially, I thought of splitting 91 into 90 + 1 and 76 into 70 + 6. Then, multiplying each part: 90*70, 90*6, 1*70, 1*6. Then, adding all those. But when I added 90*70 (6300) and 90*6 (540), that's 6300 + 540 = 6840. Then adding 1*70 (70) and 1*6 (6) gives 76. Then 6840 + 76 = 6916. So, my initial mistake was adding 6300 + 5400 instead of 6300 + 540. That was an error in arithmetic. So, important to keep track of the numbers properly. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using another method. Let's try multiplying 91 by 76 using another approach. For example, 76 can be written as 70 + 6, so 91*70 + 91*6. Let's compute 91*70 first. 91*70. 90*70=6300, 1*70=70. So, 6300 + 70 = 6370. Then, 91*6. 90*6=540, 1*6=6. So, 540 + 6 = 546. Then, adding 6370 + 546. 6370 + 500 = 6870, 6870 + 46 = 6916. So, same result. So, that's correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard algorithm again. Let's do it step by step. Multiply 91 by 76. \n\nFirst, write 91 and 76 vertically:\n\n   91\nx 76\n-------\n\nMultiply 91 by 6 (ones place):\n\n91\n  6\n-----\n546\n\nThen multiply 91 by 7 (tens place), which is 91*70:\n\n91\n  70\n-----\n6370\n\nNow, add 546 and 6370:\n\n  546\n+6370\n-------\n6916\n\nYes, that's 6916. So, that's correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use the calculator method. But since I don't have a calculator, perhaps another check. Let's see, 91*70=6370, 91*6=546. 6370+546=6916. Yep. So, that's correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 91 is 90 +1 and 76 is 70 +6, so (90+1)(70+6)=90*70 +90*6 +1*70 +1*6=6300 +540 +70 +6=6300+540=6840 +70=6910 +6=6916. So, that's the same as before. \n\nSo, all methods lead to 6916. Therefore, the product of 91 and 76 is 6916. \n\nWait, but just to make sure, let me try another way. Let's use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step. \n\nMultiply 91 by 76. \n\nStart with the ones digit of the multiplier, which is 6. Multiply 91 by 6. \n\n91\nx  6\n------\n546\n\nThat's because 90*6=540 and 1*6=6, so 540+6=546. \n\nNow, multiply 91 by the tens digit, which is 7, but since it's in the tens place, it's 70. So, 91*70. \n\n91\nx 70\n------\n6370\n\nBecause 90*70=6300 and 1*70=70, so 6300+70=6370. \n\nNow, add the two results: 546 and 6370. \n\n546\n+6370\n-------\n6916\n\nYes, adding 546 + 6370. Let's do it step by step. \n\n546 + 6000 = 6546\n\n6546 + 370 = 6916\n\nYes, that's correct. \n\nAlternatively, adding 546 + 6370:\n\nStart from the rightmost digits. 6 + 0 = 6. \n\n4 + 7 = 11. Write down 1, carry over 1. \n\n5 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 9. \n\nSo, 6916. \n\nTherefore, all methods confirm that the product is 6916. \n\nSo, the initial mistake was in the first calculation where I incorrectly added 6300 + 5400 instead of 6300 + 540. That was a simple arithmetic error. But after correcting that, all methods agree. \n\nTherefore, the answer is 6916.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 91 and 76 is \\boxed{6916}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 91 and 76, we can use the distributive property:\n\n1. Split 91 into 90 + 1 and 76 into 70 + 6.\n2. Apply the distributive property: \\((90 + 1)(70 + 6)\\).\n3. Calculate each part separately:\n   - \\(90 \\times 70 = 6300\\)\n   - \\(90 \\times 6 = 540\\)\n   - \\(1 \\times 70 = 70\\)\n   - \\(1 \\times 6 = 6\\)\n4. Add all the results together:\n   - \\(6300 + 540 + 70 + 6\\)\n   - First, add \\(6300 + 540 = 6840\\)\n   - Then, add \\(6840 + 70 = 6910\\)\n   - Finally, add \\(6910 + 6 = 6916\\)\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication method:\n1. Multiply 91 by 6 (ones digit of 76):\n   - \\(91 \\times 6 = 546\\)\n2. Multiply 91 by 70 (tens digit of 76):\n   - \\(91 \\times 70 = 6370\\)\n3. Add the results:\n   - \\(546 + 6370 = 6916\\)\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 91 and 76 is \\(\\boxed{6916}\\).",
