r. Breaking it down:\n\n14 \u00d7 30  \n= (10 + 4) \u00d7 30  \n= 10\u00d730 + 4\u00d730  \n= 300 + 120  \n= 420  \n\nAlternatively, recognizing that 14 \u00d7 30 is the same as 14 \u00d7 3 \u00d7 10:  \n14 \u00d7 3 = 42  \n42 \u00d7 10 = 420  \n\nBoth methods confirm the result.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{420}",
