62 is 2418. Oh, that's another way. So 31*80 is 2480, subtract 31*2 which is 62, gives 2418. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlright, so all these different methods are converging on 2418. I think that's solid. So the product of 31 and 78 is 2418. I can't see any mistakes in my reasoning here. Each step checks out with different multiplication techniques, so I'm confident that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 31 and 78 is \\boxed{2418}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 31 and 78, we can use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n31 \\times 78 = (30 + 1) \\times 78 = 30 \\times 78 + 1 \\times 78\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(30 \\times 78\\):\n\n\\[\n30 \\times 78 = 2340\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(1 \\times 78\\):\n\n\\[\n1 \\times 78 = 78\n\\]\n\nAdd the results together:\n\n\\[\n2340 + 78 = 2418\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method by breaking down the numbers differently:\n\n\\[\n31 \\times 78 = (31 \\times 70) + (31 \\times 8)\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\(31 \\times 70\\):\n\n\\[\n31 \\times 70 = 2170\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\(31 \\times 8\\):\n\n\\[\n31 \\times 8 = 248\n\\]\n\nAdd the results together:\n\n\\[\n2170 + 248 = 2418\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 31 and 78 is \\(\\boxed{2418}\\).",
