tiplication fact. For example, 12*30=360, 12*31=360+12=372. Correct. Alternatively, 31*10=310, 31*2=62, 310+62=372. Yep, same result.\n\nAnother way: 12*31. Let's do 12*31. 12*30=360, 12*1=12. 360+12=372. Definitely. So all different methods give me 372. I think that's solid. So the product of 12 and 31 is 372. I can't see any mistakes in my reasoning here. All the different approaches confirm the same answer, so I feel confident that's correct.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 12 and 31 is calculated by multiplying the two numbers together. Breaking it down:\n\n12 \u00d7 31  \n= 12 \u00d7 (30 + 1)  \n= (12 \u00d7 30) + (12 \u00d7 1)  \n= 360 + 12  \n= 372\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{372}",
