10 each. Alternatively, 74*100 is the same as 74*10^2, which is 7400. All these confirmations make me confident that the product is 7400.\n\nI don't think there's any trick or alternative interpretation here. The problem is straightforward multiplication. So, after all these checks, I'm pretty sure the answer is 7400.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 74 and 100 can be found by recognizing that multiplying by 100 moves the decimal point two places to the right. \n\nStarting with 74:\n- Multiplying by 10 gives 740.\n- Multiplying 740 by 10 again gives 7400.\n\nAlternatively, using the distributive property:\n- \\(74 \\times 100 = (70 + 4) \\times 100 = 70 \\times 100 + 4 \\times 100 = 7000 + 400 = 7400\\).\n\nThus, the product of 74 and 100 is \\(\\boxed{7400}\\).",
