 should be 1890.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 63 and 30 can be calculated by breaking down 30 into 3 \u00d7 10. Multiplying 63 by 3 first:\n\n63 \u00d7 3 = 189  \nThen multiplying by 10:  \n189 \u00d7 10 = 1890  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{1890}",
