. The answer is definitely 1692.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 94 and 18 is \\boxed{1692}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 94 and 18, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Straight Multiplication**:\n   - Multiply 94 by 8: \\(94 \\times 8 = 752\\)\n   - Multiply 94 by 10: \\(94 \\times 10 = 940\\)\n   - Add the results: \\(752 + 940 = 1692\\)\n\n2. **Breaking Down 18 into 10 + 8**:\n   - \\(94 \\times 10 = 940\\)\n   - \\(94 \\times 8 = 752\\)\n   - Add the results: \\(940 + 752 = 1692\\)\n\n3. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm**:\n   - Multiply 94 by 8: \\(94 \\times 8 = 752\\)\n   - Shift result one position left and multiply by 10: \\(752 \\times 10 = 7520\\)\n   - Add the results: \\(752 + 7520 = 1692\\)\n\n4. **Using 18 as 20 - 2**:\n   - \\(94 \\times 20 = 1880\\)\n   - \\(94 \\times 2 = 188\\)\n   - Subtract: \\(1880 - 188 = 1692\\)\n\n5. **Breaking Down 18 into 9 x 2**:\n   - \\(94 \\times 9 = 846\\)\n   - Multiply by 2: \\(846 \\times 2 = 1692\\)\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 94 and 18 is \\(\\boxed{1692}\\).",
