\n\\[\n2 \\times 55 = 110\n\\]\n\nSubtract the results:\n\n\\[\n5500 - 110 = 5390\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method by breaking down 55 into 50 and 5:\n\n\\[\n98 \\times 55 = 98 \\times (50 + 5) = 98 \\times 50 + 98 \\times 5\n\\]\n\nCalculate each part:\n\n\\[\n98 \\times 50 = 4900\n\\]\n\\[\n98 \\times 5 = 490\n\\]\n\nAdd the results:\n\n\\[\n4900 + 490 = 5390\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 98 and 55 is \\(\\boxed{5390}\\).",
