 times 1 is 38. So 2280 + 38 is 2318. Correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use decimal multiplication. 38.0 times 61.0. Let's do that. 38 times 61.0. \n\nBut that's the same as before. Maybe breaking down 61 into 60 +1. So 38*60=2280, 38*1=38. Sum is 2318. \n\nAlternatively, use the calculator method. If I didn't have a calculator, but I know that 38*60=2280, so 38*61=2280+38=2318. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use distributive property in another way. For example, 38*61 = (40 - 2)*61 = 40*61 - 2*61 = 2440 - 122 = 2318. \n\nYes, that's the same as before. So all different methods give me 2318. So I think that's the correct answer. \n\nWait, just to make sure, maybe do a quick check. Let's see, 38*60=2280, which is 2280. Then 38*1=38. So 2280 + 38. 2280 + 30 is 2310, plus 8 is 2318. Correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use another multiplication technique. Let's try the vertical multiplication:\n\n     38\n   x 61\n   ------\n     38  (38 x 1)\n   228   (38 x 6, shifted one position to the left)\n   ------\n   2318\n\nYes, that's the same as before. So the multiplication is correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use the difference of squares formula? Wait, 61 is 60 +1, but 38 is 40 -2. So (40 -2)(60 +1). Let's expand that. 40*60 + 40*1 -2*60 -2*1. Which is 2400 +40 -120 -2. 2400 +40 is 2440, minus 120 is 2320, minus 2 is 2318. Yep, same answer. \n\nSo all different methods confirm that the product is 2318. Therefore, I can be confident that the answer is 2318.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 38 and 61 is \\boxed{2318}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 38 and 61, we can use the distributive property. \n\nFirst, consider breaking down 38 into 40 - 2. Then, multiply each part by 61 and combine the results:\n\n\\[\n38 \\times 61 = (40 - 2) \\times 61 = 40 \\times 61 - 2 \\times 61\n\\]\n\nCalculate each part separately:\n\n1. \\(40 \\times 61\\):\n   \\[\n   40 \\times 60 = 2400 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 40 \\times 1 = 40\n   \\]\n   Adding these together:\n   \\[\n   2400 + 40 = 2440\n   \\]\n\n2. \\(2 \\times 61\\):\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 60 = 120 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 2 \\times 1 = 2\n   \\]\n   Adding these together:\n   \\[\n   120 + 2 = 122\n   \\]\n\nSubtract the second result from the first:\n\\[\n2440 - 122 = 2318\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method by breaking down 61 into 60 + 1 and multiplying separately:\n\n1. \\(38 \\times 60\\):\n   \\[\n   38 \\times 60 = 2280\n   \\]\n\n2. \\(38 \\times 1\\):\n   \\[\n   38 \\times 1 = 38\n   \\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n2280 + 38 = 2318\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 38 and 61 is \\(\\boxed{2318}\\).",
