think>\n\nTo find the product of 95 and 32, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Breaking down the numbers:**\n   - \\(95 = 90 + 5\\)\n   - \\(32 = 30 + 2\\)\n   - Using the distributive property:\n     \\[\n     (90 + 5) \\times (30 + 2) = 90 \\times 30 + 90 \\times 2 + 5 \\times 30 + 5 \\times 2\n     \\]\n     - \\(90 \\times 30 = 2700\\)\n     - \\(90 \\times 2 = 180\\)\n     - \\(5 \\times 30 = 150\\)\n     - \\(5 \\times 2 = 10\\)\n     - Adding these results: \\(2700 + 180 + 150 + 10 = 3040\\)\n\n2. **Direct multiplication:**\n   - \\(95 \\times 30 = 2850\\)\n   - \\(95 \\times 2 = 190\\)\n   - Adding these results: \\(2850 + 190 = 3040\\)\n\n3. **Using the distributive property with subtraction:**\n   - \\(95 = 100 - 5\\)\n   - \\(100 \\times 32 = 3200\\)\n   - \\(5 \\times 32 = 160\\)\n   - Subtracting these results: \\(3200 - 160 = 3040\\)\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 95 and 32 is \\(\\boxed{3040}\\).",
