\\[\n     5 \\times 48 = 240 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 240)}\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 48 by 6 (tens digit of 65):\n     \\[\n     6 \\times 48 = 288 \\quad \\text{(tens digit is 2880)}\n     \\]\n   - Combine the results:\n     \\[\n     240 + 2880 = 3120\n     \\]\n\n3. **Using the difference of squares:**\n   - Express 48 as \\(50 - 2\\):\n     \\[\n     48 \\times 65 = (50 - 2) \\times 65 = 50 \\times 65 - 2 \\times 65\n     \\]\n   - Calculate:\n     \\[\n     50 \\times 65 = 3250 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 2 \\times 65 = 130 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 3250 - 130 = 3120\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 48 and 65 is \\(\\boxed{3120}\\).",
      "logprobs": null,
