 Then subtract 162 from 2700. 2700 - 162. Let's subtract 100 first, which is 2600, then subtract 62 more: 2600 - 62 = 2538. Again, same answer. So three different methods all leading to 2538. That must be correct.\n\nI think that's solid. So the product of 54 and 47 is 2538.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 54 and 47, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. **Multiply 54 by 7** (ones digit of 47):\n   - \\( 54 \\times 7 = 378 \\)\n\n2. **Multiply 54 by 4** (tens digit of 47, remember to add a zero):\n   - \\( 54 \\times 4 = 216 \\)\n   - Add a zero: \\( 216 \\times 10 = 2160 \\)\n\n3. **Add the results**:\n   - \\( 378 + 2160 = 2538 \\)\n\n**Verification using the distributive property**:\n- \\( 54 \\times 47 = 54 \\times (40 + 7) = 54 \\times 40 + 54 \\times 7 \\)\n- \\( 54 \\times 40 = 2160 \\)\n- \\( 54 \\times 7 = 378 \\)\n- \\( 2160 + 378 = 2538 \\)\n\n**Verification using decomposition**:\n- \\( 54 \\times 47 = 54 \\times (50 - 3) = 54 \\times 50 - 54 \\times 3 \\)\n- \\( 54 \\times 50 = 2700 \\)\n- \\( 54 \\times 3 = 162 \\)\n- \\( 2700 - 162 = 2538 \\)\n\nAll methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{2538}\\).",
