      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 21 and 42. Hmm, let's see. Product means multiplication, right? So I just have to multiply 21 by 42. Alright, let me try to do this step by step.\n\nFirst, maybe I can break down 21 and 42 into smaller numbers that are easier to multiply. Let's start with 21. I know that 21 is 20 plus 1. So maybe I can use the distributive property here. That means I can multiply 20 by 42 and then add 1 times 42 together. Let me write that out:\n\n21 \u00d7 42 = (20 + 1) \u00d7 42 = 20\u00d742 + 1\u00d742\n\nOkay, so 20 times 42. Let me calculate that. 20 times 40 is 800, and 20 times 2 is 40. So adding those together, 800 + 40 = 840. Then 1 times 42 is just 42. So now I add 840 and 42. Let's see, 840 + 40 is 880, and then +2 more is 882. So that gives me 882. Wait, is that right?\n\nLet me check another way to make sure. Maybe I can multiply 21 by 42 directly. Let's do it the standard way. 21\n\u00d742\n------\nFirst, multiply 21 by 2 (the units digit of 42). 21\u00d72=42. Then multiply 21 by 40 (the tens digit of 42). 21\u00d740=840. Then add those two results together: 42 + 840 = 882. Yep, same answer. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method like the difference of squares or something, but that might be more complicated. Let me see. 42 is 6\u00d77 and 21 is 3\u00d77. So 21\u00d742 = 3\u00d77\u00d76\u00d77. That's (3\u00d76)\u00d7(7\u00d77) = 18\u00d749. Hmm, 18 times 49. Let's compute that. 18\u00d750 would be 900, but subtract 18 to get 900 - 18 = 882. So that works too. So three different methods all give me 882. That gives me confidence that the answer is correct.\n\nWait, just to be thorough, maybe I can check with addition. If I add 21 repeatedly 42 times, but that's tedious. Alternatively, maybe use a calculator. But since I don't have a calculator here, maybe I can estimate. 20\u00d740=800, 20\u00d72=40, 1\u00d740=40, 1\u00d72=2. So total is 800 + 40 + 40 + 2 = 882. Yep, same result. So all methods point to 882. I think that's solid.\n\nSo the product of 21 and 42 is 882. I don't see any mistakes in my reasoning, and multiple methods confirm the answer. So I'm pretty sure that's the right answer.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 21 and 42 is calculated by multiplying the two numbers together. Here's the step-by-step breakdown:\n\n1. **Break down 21 and 42**:\n   - \\(21 = 20 + 1\\)\n   - \\(42 = 40 + 2\\)\n\n2. **Apply the distributive property**:\n   \\[\n   21 \\times 42 = (20 + 1) \\times 42 = 20 \\times 42 + 1 \\times 42\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate each part separately**:\n   - \\(20 \\times 42 = 840\\)\n   - \\(1 \\times 42 = 42\\)\n\n4. **Add the results**:\n   \\[\n   840 + 42 = 882\n   \\]\n\n**Verification**:\n- **Standard multiplication**:\n  \\[\n  \\begin{array}{r}\n    21 \\\\\n  \\times 42 \\\\\n  \\hline\n    42 \\quad (\\text{21} \\times 2) \\\\\n  840 \\quad (\\text{21} \\times 40) \\\\\n  \\hline\n  882 \\\\\n  \\end{array}\n  \\]\n- **Alternative method (using prime factors)**:\n  \\[\n  21 \\times 42 = 3 \\times 7 \\times 6 \\times 7 = (3 \\times 6) \\times (7 \\times 7) = 18 \\times 49 = 882\n  \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the product is \\(\\boxed{882}\\).",
