0*50 is 2500, 50*3 is 150, 7*50 is 350, 7*3 is 21. Adding those up: 2500 + 150 is 2650, plus 350 is 3000, plus 21 is 3021. Yep, that's correct. So the product is 3021.\n\nAlternatively, if I do 53*57, same thing. 53*50 is 2650, 53*7 is 371. Then 2650 + 371 is 3021. Yep, same result. So that's consistent. So I think that's the right answer. 3021.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 57 and 53 is \\boxed{3021}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 57 and 53, we can use the distributive property. \n\nFirst, break down 57 into 50 + 7 and 53 into 50 + 3. Then, expand the product:\n\n\\[\n(50 + 7)(50 + 3)\n\\]\n\nExpanding this using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n50 \\cdot 50 + 50 \\cdot 3 + 7 \\cdot 50 + 7 \\cdot 3\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n\\[\n2500 + 150 + 350 + 21\n\\]\n\nAdd the results step by step:\n\n\\[\n2500 + 150 = 2650\n\\]\n\\[\n2650 + 350 = 3000\n\\]\n\\[\n3000 + 21 = 3021\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 57 and 53 is \\(\\boxed{3021}\\).",
