o the multiplication directly. Let's do 47*80. Let's write it as:\n\n      47\n   x 80\n   ----\n      3760\n\nYes, that's the same as before. So, the thousands place: 40*80=3200, hundreds place: 7*80=560, add them together: 3200+560=3760. Yep, that's correct.\n\nI think that's solid. All methods converge to 3760. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. So, the product of 47 and 80 is 3760.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 47 and 80 is \\boxed{3760}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 47 and 80, we can break down the multiplication into simpler steps. \n\nFirst, we can use the distributive property:\n\\[\n47 \\times 80 = (40 + 7) \\times 80 = 40 \\times 80 + 7 \\times 80\n\\]\n\nCalculating each part separately:\n\\[\n40 \\times 80 = 3200\n\\]\n\\[\n7 \\times 80 = 560\n\\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n3200 + 560 = 3760\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method by breaking down 80 into 8 and 10:\n\\[\n47 \\times 80 = 47 \\times (8 \\times 10) = (47 \\times 8) \\times 10\n\\]\n\nCalculating \\(47 \\times 8\\):\n\\[\n47 \\times 8 = 376\n\\]\n\nThen multiplying by 10:\n\\[\n376 \\times 10 = 3760\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 47 and 80 is \\(\\boxed{3760}\\).",
