n't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I'm confident that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 81 and 14 is \\boxed{1134}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 81 and 14, we can break it down into simpler steps:\n\n1. Multiply 81 by 10:\n   \\[\n   81 \\times 10 = 810\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 81 by 4:\n   \\[\n   81 \\times 4 = 324\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the results from steps 1 and 2:\n   \\[\n   810 + 324 = 1134\n   \\]\n\nWe can verify this using different methods, such as breaking down 14 into 10 + 3 + 1 and then adding the results, or using the standard multiplication method. All methods confirm that the product of 81 and 14 is \\(\\boxed{1134}\\).",
