      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 19 and 87. Hmm, let's see. I remember that multiplying two numbers means adding the first number to itself as many times as the second number. So, 19 times 87. Let me think how to do this step by step.\n\nFirst, maybe breaking down 87 into smaller parts would make it easier. Like, 80 plus 7. So, 19 multiplied by 80 plus 19 multiplied by 7. Let me check if that works. Yeah, because 80 + 7 is 87, so that should give the same result as multiplying them first. Let's try that.\n\nStarting with 19 times 80. Hmm, 19 times 8 is 152, right? Because 10 times 8 is 80, and 9 times 8 is 72, so 80 + 72 is 152. So, 19 times 80 would be 1520. Wait, because 152 times 10 is 1520. Yeah, that makes sense.\n\nNow, 19 times 7. Let's calculate that. 10 times 7 is 70, and 9 times 7 is 63. So, 70 + 63 is 133. So, 19 times 7 is 133.\n\nNow, add those two results together: 1520 + 133. Let's see. 1520 + 100 is 1620, and then +33 more would be 1653. So, 1520 + 133 equals 1653. Therefore, 19 times 87 is 1653. Let me verify that with another method to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, I can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Let's line them up:\n\n  19\nx 87\n-----\n\nFirst, multiply 19 by 7. 19 times 7 is 133, as before. Then multiply 19 by 80, which is 1520. Then add them together: 133 + 1520. Let's add 133 + 1520. 133 + 1500 is 1633, then +20 is 1653. Yep, same result. That seems consistent.\n\nWait, maybe another way. Let's try using distributive property differently. 87 is 80 + 7, so 19*80 + 19*7. Wait, that's what I did first. Alternatively, maybe using 19 as 20 - 1. Let's see:\n\n19 * 87 = (20 - 1) * 87 = 20*87 - 1*87. 20*87 is 1740, and 1*87 is 87. So, 1740 - 87. Let's subtract. 1740 - 80 is 1660, then subtract 7 more is 1653. Again, same answer. That's reassuring.\n\nAnother check: Let's use the fact that 19 is 10 + 9. So, 10*87 + 9*87. 10*87 is 870, 9*87 is 783. Then 870 + 783. 870 + 700 is 1570, 1570 + 83 is 1653. Same result again. Okay, so all different methods give me 1653. That gives me confidence that the answer is correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using a calculator to verify. But since I don't have a calculator here, I can do a quick check. Let's see, 20*87 is 1740, subtract 1*87 (87) gives 1740 - 87 = 1653. Yep, same as before.\n\nSo, all methods converge to 1653. Therefore, I can be pretty sure that the product of 19 and 87 is 1653. I think that's the answer. Let me just write it down properly.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 19 and 87 is \\boxed{1653}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 19 and 87, we can break down 87 into 80 and 7, then use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n19 \\times 87 = 19 \\times (80 + 7) = 19 \\times 80 + 19 \\times 7\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(19 \\times 80\\):\n\\[\n19 \\times 80 = 1520\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(19 \\times 7\\):\n\\[\n19 \\times 7 = 133\n\\]\n\nAdd the results together:\n\\[\n1520 + 133 = 1653\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method by considering \\(19\\) as \\(20 - 1\\):\n\\[\n19 \\times 87 = (20 - 1) \\times 87 = 20 \\times 87 - 1 \\times 87\n\\]\n\\[\n20 \\times 87 = 1740\n\\]\n\\[\n1 \\times 87 = 87\n\\]\n\\[\n1740 - 87 = 1653\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 19 and 87 is \\(\\boxed{1653}\\).",
