ogether: 73 + 6570. 73 + 6570. 6570 + 70 is 6640, plus 3 is 6643. Yep, same result again.\n\nWait, maybe I can check with a calculator? But since I don't have one, maybe I can check with another multiplication. Let's see, 73*91. Let's see, 70*90=6300, 70*1=70, 3*90=270, 3*1=3. So 6300+70+270+3=6300+70=6370, 6370+270=6640, 6640+3=6643. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 73*91 is equal to (70+3)(90+1) which we already did. Alternatively, maybe use the identity (a + b)(a - b) = a\u00b2 - b\u00b2, but I don't think that applies here. Let's see, 73 and 91. The average of 73 and 91 is (73 + 91)/2 = 164/2 = 82. The difference is 91 - 73 = 18. So, 82\u00b2 - 18\u00b2. Let's compute that. 82 squared is 6724, and 18 squared is 324. Then 6724 - 324 = 6400. Wait, that's not 6643. Hmm, so that doesn't work. Maybe that identity isn't applicable here. Maybe I made a mistake in the approach. Wait, 82 squared is 6724, 18 squared is 324. 6724 - 324 is 6400. But 6400 is not 6643. So that method doesn't work here. Maybe that identity isn't helpful here. So scratch that.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method. Let's try breaking down 91 into 100 - 9. So 73*(100 - 9) = 73*100 - 73*9 = 7300 - 657. Then subtract 657 from 7300. 7300 - 600 is 6700, 6700 - 57 is 6643. There we go. So that works. So 73*91 = 7300 - 657 = 6643. That's another way to get the same answer. So that's consistent.\n\nSo all methods point to 6643. Let me just verify once more with another approach. Let's use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step.\n\nMultiplying 73 by 91:\n\nStart with the units digit of 91, which is 1. Multiply 73 by 1: 73. Write that down.\n\nNext, multiply 73 by the tens digit of 91, which is 9. But since it's the tens place, it's 73*9*10. So 73*9: 70*9=630, 3*9=27, so 630+27=657. Then multiply by 10: 657*10=6570. Write that next to the previous result.\n\nNow, add the two numbers: 73 + 6570. Let's add 73 + 6570. 6570 + 70 = 6640, then 6640 + 3 = 6643. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the vertical multiplication method:\n\n      73\n    x91\n    ----\n      73  (73 x 1)\n     657   (73 x 9, shifted one position to the left)\n    ----\n     6643  (Adding 73 and 6570)\n\nYes, that's the same as before. So all methods confirm that the product is 6643. I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. So the answer should be 6643.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 73 and 91 is \\boxed{6643}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 73 and 91, we can use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n73 \\times 91 = 73 \\times (90 + 1) = 73 \\times 90 + 73 \\times 1\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(73 \\times 90\\):\n\n\\[\n73 \\times 90 = 73 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 657 \\times 10 = 6570\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(73 \\times 1\\):\n\n\\[\n73 \\times 1 = 73\n\\]\n\nAdd the results together:\n\n\\[\n6570 + 73 = 6643\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using another method by breaking down 91 into 100 - 9:\n\n\\[\n73 \\times 91 = 73 \\times (100 - 9) = 73 \\times 100 - 73 \\times 9 = 7300 - 657\n\\]\n\nSubtract the results:\n\n\\[\n7300 - 657 = 6643\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 73 and 91 is \\(\\boxed{6643}\\).",
