vercomplicating. Let me think. The exact difference would be (70-3)(60-2) = 70*60 - 70*2 - 3*60 + 3*2 = 4200 - 140 - 180 + 6 = 4200 - 320 + 6 = 3886. Oh, that works! So that's another way to get 3886. So all methods confirm that the product is 3886. I think that's solid. So the answer should be 3886.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 67 and 58 is \\boxed{3886}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 67 and 58, we can use the distributive property:\n\n1. Break down 67 into 60 + 7 and 58 into 50 + 8.\n2. Distribute the multiplication:\n   - \\(60 \\times 50 = 3000\\)\n   - \\(60 \\times 8 = 480\\)\n   - \\(7 \\times 50 = 350\\)\n   - \\(7 \\times 8 = 56\\)\n3. Add all the results together:\n   - \\(3000 + 480 + 350 + 56 = 3886\\)\n\nWe can verify this using another method:\n1. Multiply 67 by 58 using the standard algorithm:\n   - \\(8 \\times 67 = 536\\)\n   - \\(50 \\times 67 = 3350\\)\n   - Add the results: \\(536 + 3350 = 3886\\)\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 67 and 58 is \\(\\boxed{3886}\\).",
