nswer**\nThe product of 93 and 58 is \\boxed{5394}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 93 and 58, we can use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n93 \\times 58 = (90 + 3) \\times (50 + 8)\n\\]\n\nFirst, distribute the multiplication over addition:\n\n1. Multiply 90 by 50: \\(90 \\times 50 = 4500\\)\n2. Multiply 90 by 8: \\(90 \\times 8 = 720\\)\n3. Multiply 3 by 50: \\(3 \\times 50 = 150\\)\n4. Multiply 3 by 8: \\(3 \\times 8 = 24\\)\n\nNext, add all these results together:\n\n\\[\n4500 + 720 + 150 + 24\n\\]\n\nAdding step by step:\n\n1. \\(4500 + 720 = 5220\\)\n2. \\(5220 + 150 = 5370\\)\n3. \\(5370 + 24 = 5394\\)\n\nTo verify, we can use another method by breaking down the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n93 \\times 58 = 93 \\times (50 + 8) = 93 \\times 50 + 93 \\times 8\n\\]\n\n1. Calculate \\(93 \\times 50\\): \\(93 \\times 50 = 4650\\)\n2. Calculate \\(93 \\times 8\\): \\(93 \\times 8 = 744\\)\n\nAdding these results:\n\n\\[\n4650 + 744 = 5394\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 93 and 58 is \\(\\boxed{5394}\\).",
