confidence that the answer is correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication algorithm. Let's write it out:\n\n   74\nx 39\n-----\n  666  (74 x 9)\n2220   (74 x 30, shifted one position to the left)\n-----\n2886\n\nAdding 666 and 2220 gives 2886. Yep, that's the same as before. So all methods converge to 2886. Therefore, I can be pretty sure that the product of 74 and 39 is 2886.\n\nJust to make sure, maybe do a quick check with a calculator. Wait, since I don't have a calculator here, but I can estimate. 70*40 is 2800, which is a bit higher than 2886, but since 74 is 4 more than 70 and 39 is 1 less than 40, the difference should be manageable. Let's see, the actual product is 2886, which is 2800 + 86. Since 74 is 4 more than 70, and 39 is 1 less than 40, the total difference is 4*40 -1*70 = 160 -70 =90. Wait, but how does that relate? Maybe not the easiest way. Alternatively, the difference between 70*40 and 70*40 -70 +160 -4. Hmm, maybe not. But since all the step-by-step methods give the same answer, and the alternative methods as well, I think 2886 is correct.\n\nSo, after all these checks, I'm confident that the product of 74 and 39 is 2886.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 74 and 39 is \\boxed{2886}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 74 and 39, we can use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n74 \\times 39 = (70 + 4)(40 - 1)\n\\]\n\nExpanding this using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n= 70 \\times 40 + 70 \\times (-1) + 4 \\times 40 + 4 \\times (-1)\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n\\[\n70 \\times 40 = 2800\n\\]\n\\[\n70 \\times (-1) = -70\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\times 40 = 160\n\\]\n\\[\n4 \\times (-1) = -4\n\\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\n\\[\n2800 - 70 + 160 - 4\n\\]\n\nFirst, compute \\(2800 - 70\\):\n\n\\[\n2800 - 70 = 2730\n\\]\n\nThen, add 160:\n\n\\[\n2730 + 160 = 2890\n\\]\n\nFinally, subtract 4:\n\n\\[\n2890 - 4 = 2886\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can also use another method by breaking down 39 into 40 - 1:\n\n\\[\n74 \\times 39 = 74 \\times (40 - 1) = 74 \\times 40 - 74 \\times 1\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n\\[\n74 \\times 40 = 2960\n\\]\n\\[\n74 \\times 1 = 74\n\\]\n\nSubtracting these results:\n\n\\[\n2960 - 74 = 2886\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 74 and 39 is \\(\\boxed{2886}\\).",
