at's the correct result.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 43 and 52 can be calculated using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n43 \\times 52 = (40 + 3)(50 + 2)\n\\]\n\nFirst, distribute the multiplication:\n\n- \\(40 \\times 50 = 2000\\)\n- \\(40 \\times 2 = 80\\)\n- \\(3 \\times 50 = 150\\)\n- \\(3 \\times 2 = 6\\)\n\nAdd the results together:\n\n\\[\n2000 + 80 + 150 + 6 = 2236\n\\]\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication method confirms the result. \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{2236}",
