think again.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the formula (a + b)(a - b) = a\u00b2 - b\u00b2, but 93 and 79 aren't that close. Hmm, 93 is 90 + 3, 79 is 80 -1. So maybe (90 + 3)(80 -1) which is what I did earlier. So that gives 90*80 -90 + 3*80 -3. Which is 7200 -90 +240 -3. Which is 7200 + ( -90 +240 ) -3 = 7200 + 150 -3 = 7347. Yeah, that's the same as before.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another multiplication technique. Let's try multiplying 93 by 79 step by step. 93*79. Let's do 93*80 and then subtract 93. So 93*80 is 7440. Then subtract 93: 7440 - 93. 7440 - 90 is 7350, then subtract 3 more is 7347. Yep, same answer again. So that's three different methods giving me 7347. That gives me confidence that the answer is correct.\n\nBut just to be thorough, let me check with a calculator. Wait, I don't have a calculator here, but maybe I can compute 93*79 using another method. Let's see. 93*79. Let's break 79 into 70 + 9. So 93*70 is 6510, and 93*9 is 837. Then 6510 + 837. Let's add 6510 + 800 = 7310, then add 37: 7310 + 37 = 7347. Yep, same result. So all methods point to 7347.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 93 is 90 + 3 and 79 is 80 -1, so (90 +3)(80 -1) = 90*80 -90 +240 -3 = 7200 +150 -3 = 7347. Yep, same.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n     93\n   x 79\n   ----\n     837  (93 x 9)\n   6510   (93 x 70, shifted one position to the left)\n   ----\n   7347\n\nAdding 837 and 6510 gives 7347. Correct.\n\nSo all methods confirm that the product is 7347. Therefore, I can be confident that the answer is 7347.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 93 and 79 is \\boxed{7347}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 93 and 79, we can use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n93 \\times 79 = (90 + 3)(80 - 1)\n\\]\n\nExpanding this expression:\n\n\\[\n(90 + 3)(80 - 1) = 90 \\times 80 + 90 \\times (-1) + 3 \\times 80 + 3 \\times (-1)\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n\\[\n90 \\times 80 = 7200\n\\]\n\\[\n90 \\times (-1) = -90\n\\]\n\\[\n3 \\times 80 = 240\n\\]\n\\[\n3 \\times (-1) = -3\n\\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\n\\[\n7200 - 90 + 240 - 3 = 7200 + (240 - 90) - 3 = 7200 + 150 - 3 = 7347\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify this by direct multiplication:\n\n\\[\n93 \\times 79 = 93 \\times (80 - 1) = 93 \\times 80 - 93 \\times 1\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n\\[\n93 \\times 80 = 7440\n\\]\n\\[\n93 \\times 1 = 93\n\\]\n\nSubtracting these results:\n\n\\[\n7440 - 93 = 7347\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 93 and 79 is \\(\\boxed{7347}\\).",
