ultiplier 75 into 7 +5 instead of 70 +5. That was the error.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 3300. But wait, let me check with a calculator to be sure. Let me compute 44 \u00d775.\n\n44 multiplied by 75. Let's compute 44\u00d770=3080, 44\u00d75=220. 3080+220=3300. Yes, that's correct. Alternatively, 75\u00d744. 75\u00d740=3000, 75\u00d74=300. 3000+300=3300. So, that's another way to compute. 75\u00d740=3000, 75\u00d74=300, so total 3300. So, that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 44 and 75 is 3300. So, the initial mistake was in the first method where I split 75 into 7 +5 instead of 70 +5, leading to an incorrect sum. Therefore, the correct answer is 3300.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 44 and 75 is \\boxed{3300}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 44 and 75, we can break down the multiplication using the distributive property:\n\n1. Break down 75 into 70 and 5:\n   \\[\n   44 \\times 75 = 44 \\times (70 + 5)\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 44 by each component:\n   \\[\n   44 \\times 70 = 3080 \\quad \\text{(since } 44 \\times 7 = 308 \\text{ and then multiplied by 10)}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   44 \\times 5 = 220\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the results of the two multiplications:\n   \\[\n   3080 + 220 = 3300\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 44 and 75 is \\(\\boxed{3300}\\).",
