0. \n\nLet me check with another method. Let's use the standard multiplication algorithm. \n\nMultiply 87 by 10. \n\nStarting from the rightmost digit: 7 times 10 is 70. Write down 0 and carry over 7. \n\nThen the leftmost digit: 8 times 10 is 80, plus the carried over 7 is 87. \n\nSo writing it down, you get 870. \n\nYes, that works. So all methods lead to 870. \n\nI think that's solid. So the product of 87 and 10 is 870. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 87 and 10 is \\boxed{870}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 87 and 10, we can use the fact that multiplying a number by 10 simply adds a zero to the end of the number. \n\n1. Start with the number 87.\n2. Multiply by 10: \\( 87 \\times 10 = 870 \\).\n\nVerification using the distributive property:\n- Split 87 into 80 and 7.\n- Calculate \\( 80 \\times 10 = 800 \\) and \\( 7 \\times 10 = 70 \\).\n- Add the results: \\( 800 + 70 = 870 \\).\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n- Multiply the rightmost digit (7) by 10: \\( 7 \\times 10 = 70 \\) (write down 0 and carry over 7).\n- Multiply the leftmost digit (8) by 10: \\( 8 \\times 10 = 80 \\), then add the carried over 7: \\( 80 + 7 = 87 \\).\n- Combine the results: 870.\n\nThus, the product of 87 and 10 is \\(\\boxed{870}\\).",
